		{"id":"1c7800c6e0a921df","type":"text","text":"### Retrieval of memory\n- Perform after each section or chapter\n- From memory, rebuild schemata as best as possible. Then refine\n- Strengthens memory recall and can rebuild schemata and more organized format\n- Revise after with previous schemata.","x":115,"y":-20,"width":441,"height":320},
		{"id":"f3b4dbab78e96ed1","type":"text","text":"### Create Schemata\n- When going over content, write down key words and concepts.\n- Create schemata with connections and relationships.\n- Explain in own words with connections to prior knowledge.\n- Schemata DOESN'T have to be correct or organized.\n- JUST JOT DOWN AND CONNECT.","x":-320,"y":-20,"width":380,"height":320},
		{"id":"6553631e0998f6fa","type":"text","text":"### Take unnecessary load of the mind\n- Minimize environmental distractions.\n- Create a clear goal.\n- Get a lay of the land before diving into new content.","x":-645,"y":-15,"width":268,"height":315},
		{"id":"2ff934e7102b8105","type":"text","text":"### Cognitive Overload Theory and Time Management\n- Work in time chunks of 1 hour with a 10 min break\n- Prevent Cognitive Overload","x":783,"y":-20,"width":293,"height":320},
		{"id":"4fc2e8b4e5463293","type":"text","text":"### Keep a constant mental struggle\n- Constantly ask question when going through new content\n- Don't passively read.\n- Build schemata in own though process.\n- Correct work and compare against content.","x":1119,"y":-17,"width":360,"height":317}
